      "value": "One of the people rightly pointed out a small \"dilemma\" with this layout.\n\n> It's odd to send an invitation in the location. On the left is the user interaction window. On the right is their location window.\n\nAnd that's true.\n\nHowever, as I described above, due to the previous interface, we instinctively click the left side when trying to join, which can lead to sending an invitation rather than joining.\n\nThis change is more aimed at changing habits until a better layout of the profile buttons is found.\n\nThis can also be interpreted as \"Invite people from this location,\" which makes the button's appearance \"not so strange\"",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
